            "notes": "![Image](https://i.imgur.com/rv329pH.jpg)**\u26a1 Round 5 \u2013 Stacking Chaos & Maximum Menace \u26a1**\n\nBy now, you should have your full build or at least **~40% CDR**. At this point, it\u2019s all about stacking cooldown reduction to spam clones and throw suzus like confetti \ud83c\udf89. You\u2019re no longer just annoying\u2014you\u2019re a walking calamity.\n\nNowwwwww\u2014time for a power move with  [Crossing Guard](item_bb5252fd-fc6b-4dce-a60a-21b0a0add68f) ! \ud83d\ude31 **Slowing enemies by 50% movement speed** is basically turning them into turtles \ud83d\udc22. Even a blind soldier could hit them. **Officially it says 2 seconds,** but somehow **it feels like time itself slows**\u2014they\u2019re often slowed for almost the entire duration of your Kitsune. Absolute nightmare for the enemy..\n\n**\u2728 Alternative Option \u2013  [Cleansing Charge](item_4721f307-30d2-4fc1-a10b-6de7141deb68) :** If the enemy has Ashe burn or other debuffs, you can pick Cleansing Charge to remove negative effects and charge your ultimate faster. However, personally, I consider slowing enemies with Crossing Guard to be the real **game changer.**\n\n**REMEBER:**\n\n**\u23f1\ufe0f Clone & Suzu Spam:** With insane CDR, clones are popping constantly. Suzus flying everywhere. The enemy can\u2019t even track what\u2019s real.\n\n**\ud83d\udca5  [Hardlight Accelerator](item_0390c8af-2a68-4da2-b876-93da32c3f448) :** Even if you don\u2019t consistently hit 3 stacks,** having a 1 or 2 stacks is enough for a +10% on your Kunais **. Perfect for poking the enemy tank or going for a sneaky pick.\n\n**\ud83c\udf69 Team Priority:** Damage is tempting, but never forget your donuts & clone spawns. Healing your team while confusing the enemy is what keeps you the true menace.\n\n**\ud83d\udca1 Pro Tip:** Keep juggling poke, **healing, and clone placement.** A well-placed suzu + donut + clone combo can turn you into an angel for your team while driving the enemy insane \ud83d\ude08\u2728.",
